# Client boundaries

Default to **Server Components**. Use `"use client"` only for:

- `useState` / `useEffect`
- event handlers (`onClick`, `onChange`)
- browser APIs

## Pattern

```tsx
// Server: Section.tsx
export default function ModelsSection() {
  return (
    <section aria-labelledby="models-heading">
      <h2 id="models-heading">...</h2>
      <ModelsSectionClient />
    </section>
  );
}

// Client: ModelsSectionClient.tsx
"use client";
export default function ModelsSectionClient() { /* state + handlers */ }
```

- One client boundary per interactive section (`*Client.tsx`).
- Child UI without its own `"use client"` may live in separate files if only imported by the client parent.
- Prefer shared client sections (e.g. `StepsTabsSection`) over duplicating tab logic.

# Accessibility

- `<section aria-labelledby="...">` with matching heading `id`.
- `aria-hidden="true"` on decorative backgrounds and icons.
- Interactive lists: `<ul className="list-none">` + `<li>`.
- Tabs: `role="tablist"`, `role="tab"`, `role="tabpanel"`, `aria-selected`, `aria-controls`.
- Forms: visible label or `sr-only` + `htmlFor` / `id`.
